💡 **SUGGESTION: the stale preset wording survives in the test mirror (round-1 thread 3, half-applied)**

The round-1 fix reworded the library comment correctly (`tui_status_line.dart` now says the pair was *added* after `session_name` and that "fa's default preset never carried `context_total`") — but this test still carries the exact wording the thread flagged:

```dart
// gh-1762: the duplicated trailing context-window label gives way
// to the live rate pair — both render hidden until data exists, so
// the idle band keeps its pre-gh-1762 width.
```

v0's default right side was exactly `['session_name']` — nothing "gives way" here, and a reader still hunts for a deleted `context_total` that never existed in this preset. Suggest mirroring the lib comment, e.g.:

```dart
// gh-1762: the default band gains the live rate pair after the session
// name — both render hidden until data exists, so the idle band keeps
// its pre-gh-1762 width.
```

