💡 **SUGGESTION: `rateWindowMs` has no upper bound**

The strict parse rejects non-positive and non-integer values (good), but any positive int is accepted. The window length is also the sample-queue retention: `_prune` retires samples only once they age past `windowMs`, so `rateWindowMs: 10000000` (~2.8 h) makes the queue keep one entry per streamed delta — text, thinking, and tool-arg fragments alike — for the whole window, and the "live rate" stops being a rate. Marathon sessions are a known growth failure family in this repo (gh-1745: a session file grew to 1 GB from unrotated dumps), so an unbounded knob feeding a per-delta queue deserves a bound.

Suggest clamping or rejecting at parse time, e.g.:

```dart
if (rateWindowMs != null &&
    (rateWindowMs is! int || rateWindowMs <= 0 || rateWindowMs > 60000)) {
  throw ConfigException(
    '"tui.statusLine.rateWindowMs" must be an integer in (0, 60000]',
  );
}
```

or documenting the accepted range next to the knob.

